## Why

Three real Aerochrome field frames exposed four tightly related weaknesses: deep-shadow collapse, hard highlight clipping, overly uniform red areas, and noisy/partially contaminated sky treatment.

The existing engine already had a reversal-film S-curve, headroom-limited saturation, tone-preserving foliage colourization, wide sky smoothing, structured grain, and dither. This PR therefore avoids stacking another generic filter and applies a surgical scene-to-film refinement.

## Implementation

### 1. Pre-film scene curve

- applies before synthetic NIR/material rendering;
- operates on luminance while preserving chromaticity;
- anchors middle grey at 0.5;
- lifts deep shadows slightly;
- compresses source highlights;
- uses identical shaping for render and classification inputs.

Monochrome IR receives only a very small shared input shape because its H&D curve already supplies the main stock response. Aerochrome receives the stronger reversal-film input shoulder.

### 2. Red texture and highlight behavior

- retains restrained source detail inside foliage/petals;
- moves bright reds toward a paler dye response before max-red clipping;
- selectively tapers saturation only in red-dominant highlights;
- protects neutrals, skin, water, and sky from a global red correction;
- keeps red scaling within hue-preserving channel headroom.

### 3. Highlight rolloff

- protects the existing Aerochrome toe instead of replacing the tuned S-curve;
- adds a final hue-preserving shoulder after intensity/manual controls and bloom;
- leaves values below the shoulder knee unchanged;
- rolls extreme values asymptotically instead of depending on a destructive final clamp.

### 4. Sky handling

- applies an explicit vegetation veto before sky colourization;
- builds the wide sky blur entirely in raw texture space, then normalizes/precurves it once;
- uses less per-pixel detail in clear blue sky while retaining more cloud detail;
- reduces classification-mask noise;
- reduces Aerochrome grain amplitude inside classified sky while retaining final dither.

## Why no RNI purchase is required

The target is not undocumented imitation of a proprietary preset. Validation is based on measurable photographic behavior: highlight continuity, shadow separation, red texture, material assignment, sky-gradient stability, neutral preservation, and consistency across Standard, JPEG HDR, and True RAW HDR.

## Automated verification

- CPU reference math added for the scene curve, protected toe, output shoulder, and red-highlight saturation scale.
- Unit tests cover the 0.5 midpoint anchor, monotonic bounds, shadow lift, highlight compression, toe separation, shoulder behavior, and selective red desaturation.
- Final corrected source passed `testDebugUnitTest`, `assembleDebug`, and `assembleRelease` in the verified integration workflow.
- Android CI run 230 also passed the complete unit/debug/release/signing suite before the final one-line sky-domain correction.
- Ordinary Android CI run 233 is queued for the current head and will publish the installable debug artifact.

## Version

- `1.19.1`
- `versionCode 48`

## Important limitation

This can roll and preserve information that reaches the app. It cannot reconstruct sensor/ISP detail already clipped in a Standard JPEG with the sun in frame, nor remove physical optical flare. Computational HDR or True RAW HDR remains the correct source mode for severe backlight.

## Device validation target

Reprocess or re-shoot the three submitted diagnostic compositions:

1. red flowers/foliage against bright architecture and sky;
2. direct sun and flare with deep foreground shadow;
3. mixed architecture, clouds, red foliage, white fabric, and blue reflections.

Pass only when:

- petals/leaves retain internal density instead of becoming solid max-red;
- red highlights become slightly paler rather than clipping;
- deep shadows gain separation without a grey HDR wash;
- middle-grey architecture and white fabric remain stable;
- clear sky is smoother while clouds retain structure;
- foliage is never partially recoloured as sky;
- extreme brightness rolls smoothly;
- Classic, Soft, Dense, Gold, and Faded retain their established hierarchy;
- monochrome IR remains materially unchanged apart from the deliberately tiny shared input shape.

Human-UX correction from the 2026-07-23 Playwright audit.

- automatically expands a newly mounted application workflow once;
- immediately loads the application record in Overview;
- preserves normal user control after the first expansion, so the section can still be collapsed;
- removes the large blank workspace state shown in the audit screenshot;
- keeps the behavior scoped to the application workspace Overview panel.

Merge only after exact-head CI passes. A final Playwright rerun should verify the Overview workflow is visibly expanded.

